<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Constantinople (1700)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1686-1700">Russo-Turkish War (1686–1700)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Constantinople of July 1700 ended the war of 1686–1700 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Russia kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azov">Azov</a>, taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> in 1696, and Muscovy was released from paying the annual 'gifts' to the Crimean khans. The thirty-year truce freed Peter to begin the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>.</p></div>
